const decisions={
 'Control Plane':['Recognize policy/access/routing control separately from forwarded user traffic in this deck’s Zero Trust context.','Qualified as high-level Zero Trust control/decision vocabulary only. The management-layer wording does not approve a universal merger of networking management and control planes.','No product-specific control-plane design, routing protocol operation, universal plane taxonomy or authenticated access implementation.'],
 'Data Plane':['Recognize the user-traffic forwarding role under supplied control decisions.','Qualified as bounded forwarding-versus-control vocabulary.','No claim that every inspection/control function is off-path or that forwarding alone authorizes a request.'],
 'Microsegmentation':['Recognize fine-grained isolation as a strategy to limit lateral movement.','Qualified as a goal requiring actual fine-grained enforcement; dividing or naming zones alone is insufficient.','No VLAN-label-only sufficiency, guaranteed attack prevention or complete Zero Trust architecture; enforcing policy/plugin/identity is design dependent.'],
 'Defense-in-Depth':['Recognize multiple protective layers that can contain failure of one control.','Qualified as a layered-security strategy, not a guarantee under shared failure or bypass.','No independence, complete coverage, operational efficacy or guarantee every single failure is contained.'],
 'Perimeter Security':['Recognize historical boundary-oriented trust assumptions, but the category is overgeneralized.','HOLD: the full category is defined as trusting internal traffic more; boundary protections can coexist with resource-based Zero Trust without implicit internal trust.','Historical examples do not make location-based trust a requirement of every perimeter protection. No definition rewrite or child/deck approval transfer.'],
 'Shared Responsibility Model':['Recognize provider infrastructure duties alongside continuing customer data, identity and configuration duties.','Qualified as a high-level split; exact duties vary by service model, contract and selected service.','Provider also has configured-service security duties; IaaS customers may own guest OS, application and dependency patching. No complete IaaS/PaaS/SaaS duty matrix or compliance finding.'],
 'Public Cloud':['Identify that third-party ownership and internet access alone do not define public cloud.','HOLD: the definition omits provisioning for open use by the general public; ownership and access path are insufficient distinguishing criteria.','Public cloud may have business, academic, government or combined ownership; public availability is not a claim every workload/data resource is public.'],
 'Private Cloud':['Recognize cloud infrastructure for one organization with on- or off-premises hosting.','Qualified as single-organization cloud vocabulary; exclusive organizational use is the boundary.','A dedicated ordinary server is not automatically cloud; no inferred owner/operator, physical location guarantee or NIST essential-characteristic assessment.'],
 'Hybrid Cloud':['Identify missing composition and portability criteria in the connected on-prem/public shorthand.','HOLD: ordinary on-premises resources plus public services do not necessarily form distinct cloud infrastructures bound for data/application portability.','Preserve earlier hybrid-cloud section and qualification holds. Public cloud is not mandatory in every NIST private/community/public composition. No clearer neighbor transfers approval.'],
 'Community Cloud':['Recognize a shared cloud community with common mission, policy, compliance or security needs.','Qualified as cloud provisioned for the specified community, not all general public consumers.','Ownership/operation can be organizational, third-party or combined; common concerns are not demonstrated compliance or guaranteed stronger security.'],
 'FaaS':['Recognize provider-managed servers executing event-driven functions.','Qualified as serverless execution vocabulary, not outsourcing every customer security duty.','Customers still own relevant code/dependencies, permissions, data, secrets and configuration; runtime responsibilities vary. No all-functions-only-trigger or deployment guarantee.'],
 'HA':['Recognize availability as an architecture goal supported by redundancy and failover.','Qualified as the stated goal, not an observed uptime or recovery commitment.','Shared failures, detection, capacity and failover can defeat availability; backups and disaster recovery remain distinct. No 100% uptime, zero RTO/RPO or tested failover.'],
 'RAID':['Recognize multiple-disk performance and/or redundancy dependent on RAID level.','Qualified with the explicit level-dependent boundary; RAID0 gives performance without disk-failure redundancy.','RAID is not backup or immunity to deletion/corruption/ransomware; controller/common failures and rebuild risks remain. No level recommendation, restore or disk test.'],
 'ZTA':['Recognize the slogan but hold the isolated architecture definition.','HOLD: never-trust/always-verify plus continuous checks does not state resource access authorization or removal of implicit trust based on network location/ownership.','Continuous checks are not alone a complete architecture or universal every-moment check; identity/authentication alone does not authorize access. Acronym expansion does not repair the definition.']
};
